 34AR c  2020Ia01: a 30-MeV/nucleon {+35}Cl beam was produced from the K500     
 34AR2c  cyclotron at Texas A&M University and impinged on a                    
 34AR3c  liquid-nitrogen-cooled hydrogen gas target. The fully stripped reaction
 34AR4c  products recoiled into the Momentum Achromat Recoil Spectrometer       
 34AR5c  (MARS), where they were spatially separated according to their         
 34AR6c  charge-to-mass ratio. A 99.5% pure {+34}Ar beam was implanted into     
 34AR7c  aluminized Mylar tape and moved to a well-shielded location, where a   
 34AR8c  4|p proportional gas counter was used for detecting positrons. A total 
 34AR9c  of 1.7|*10{+8} decay positrons were recorded. Measured E|b, |b(t).     
 34ARAc  Deduced T{-1/2} of {+34}Ar.                                            
 34AR c  2020Ia02: similar {+34}Ar production setup at MARS. A 99.6% pure       
 34AR2c  {+34}Ar beam was implanted into aluminized Mylar tape and moved to the 
 34AR3c  counting location, where a 1-mm-thick BC-404 scintillator was used to  
 34AR4c  detect positrons and a HPGe detector was used to detect |g rays.       
 34AR5c  Measured E|b, E|g, |b(t), |g(t), |b|g coin. A total of                 
 34AR6c  2.6710(20)|*10{+8} decay positrons were recorded.                      
